    "q-36479": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36479",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of ${R}_{8}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $8?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{8}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{8}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{8}[t])=8+1=9.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
