      "kp_id": "e-8315"
    },
    "q-106875": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106875",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{5\\times 1}(R),$ the vector space of all $5\\times 1$ matrices over $R?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nThus, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{5\\times 1}(R)$ contains $5\\cdot 1=5$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{5\\times 1}(R),$ we have, indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5\\times 1}(R))=5\\cdot 1=5.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
