    "q-106900": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106900",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $3?$\n\nI. ${R}^{2}$\n\nII. ${R}_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2$\n\nIII. ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{2})=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{2}[t])=2+1=3.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
